# API wiring for the two coding-agent harnesses and the optional VLM judge.
# This is the ONLY file a runner fills in. Copy it OUTSIDE the repository:
#
#   cp .gb_api.env.example ~/.config/gamebench/gb_api.env   # then fill, then:
#   ./setup.sh --check-auth                                  # one non-billed probe per key
#
# Search order (first hit wins): $GB_API_ENV → ~/.config/gamebench/gb_api.env
# → /tmp/swe-game/.gb_api.env.
# The file is sourced by bash with `set -a`: KEY=VALUE, `export KEY=VALUE` and
# `unset KEY` lines all work. Key values never reach run logs: the harness
# redacts every value whose name contains KEY / SECRET / TOKEN, Codex gets the
# key by variable NAME (`env_key`), and the model's shells cannot see it.
# Leave a line empty (or commented) to get the "official" behaviour described
# below. `--dry-run` reads this file only for routing and never needs a key.

# --- Codex CLI harness (--harness codex) ----------------------------------------
# Empty = Codex's own ChatGPT login: run `codex login` once as the user that
# runs run_benchmark.sh; the harness copies ~/.codex/auth.json into a private
# CODEX_HOME per cell. Filled = API-key auth (Codex env_key=OPENAI_API_KEY).
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Empty = official api.openai.com. Set it to route Codex through a gateway;
# the harness then passes the provider block on the command line
# (-c model_provider="gamebench_proxy" -c model_providers.gamebench_proxy.base_url=…
#  -c model_providers.gamebench_proxy.env_key="OPENAI_API_KEY" … wire_api="responses")
# and never touches ~/.codex/config.toml. Codex CLI only speaks the Responses
# API (POST {base}/responses); a chat-completions-only gateway (Moonshot,
# DashScope, most OpenAI-compatible relays) needs a Responses translation proxy
# in front of it. `./setup.sh --check-auth` tells you which case you have.
OPENAI_BASE_URL=

# --- Claude Code harness (--harness claude) ---------------------------------------
# Both are exported into the agent's environment only (private CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
# per cell; ~/.claude is never read or written).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Use instead of ANTHROPIC_API_KEY when the endpoint wants `Authorization: Bearer`
# (e.g. Moonshot/Kimi's Anthropic-compatible endpoint documents this name).
# Claude Code reads it natively; with ANTHROPIC_API_KEY empty the route and
# `./setup.sh --check-auth` use it (the probe then sends a Bearer header).
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=
# Empty = official api.anthropic.com. Any Anthropic-compatible endpoint works
# here, e.g. Moonshot's lets Claude Code run kimi-k3
# (ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.moonshot.ai/anthropic, key in ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
#  or ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN, --model kimi-k3). Include no /v1 suffix; Claude Code
#  appends /v1/messages.
ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=

# --- Optional game-rubric VLM judge for independent evaluate.sh ------------------
# Modes 1-3 default to modeN-vlm1: 85 objective + 15 visual points. Without a
# complete VLM reading the composite is null. Calls are off by default.
# run_benchmark.sh --visual-judge vlm uses that cell's agent route instead.
# Choose the judge endpoint, model and key variable explicitly for standalone
# evaluation and --judge-visuals. Keep actual keys in this external file only.
# GAMEBENCH_VLM_PROVIDER=responses
# GAMEBENCH_VLM_MODEL=gpt-6-astra
# GAMEBENCH_VLM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# GAMEBENCH_VLM_KEY_ENV=OPENAI_API_KEY
# Set OPENAI_API_KEY above and uncomment all four judge settings to use this
# example. Keep the endpoint and key variable explicit for standalone judging.

# --- Historical GameCraft-adapted visual1 judge ---------------------------------
# Only for --registry 2026-09-11.visual1 or retained historical visual1 reports.
# Current game-rubric VLM reports use the configuration above, including when
# --judge-visuals is used. This historical judge speaks Chat Completions.
# GAMECRAFT_BENCH_JUDGE_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GAMECRAFT_BENCH_JUDGE_OPENAI_BASE_URL=
# GAMECRAFT_BENCH_JUDGE_MODEL=gpt-5.6-sol

# --- Additional routing aliases ------------------------------------------------
# Set OPENAI_BASE_URL explicitly when using a custom provider.
# GB_CODEX_BASE_URL=       # alias of OPENAI_BASE_URL      GB_CODEX_KEY_ENV=  (key var NAME)
# GB_CLAUDE_BASE_URL=      # alias of ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL   GB_CLAUDE_KEY_ENV= (key var NAME)
# scripts/run_coding.sh only: GB_CODEX_MODEL / GB_CLAUDE_MODEL (run_benchmark.sh takes --model).

# --- Proxies -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# The coding agent inherits this environment. If the machine exports *_proxy to a
# proxy the endpoint is NOT reachable through, unset them here:
# unset http_proxy https_proxy HTTP_PROXY HTTPS_PROXY all_proxy ALL_PROXY
